# Which tests a change can affect (#218), read by ci/affected.py. Reviewed like code.
#
#   pattern | crates | suites
#
# A changed file selects the union of every rule it matches. A file in a workspace crate always
# selects that crate; ci/affected.py adds every crate that depends on a selected one (normal, dev
# and build dependencies). `-` is none, `all` is everything.
#
# A file no rule matches selects every suite (and, outside the crates, every crate): add a rule
# when a path is safe to narrow, never a catch-all. `*` stays within a directory, `**` crosses
# them, and a pattern without a slash matches the file name anywhere.
#
# Suites: docs (check-public, Markdown links),
# policy (SymCC policy diffs), smoke, hibernate, restore, acceptance (local flows), daemon-uids,
# install-test, and, run by local gates and nightly, not on PRs: node-e2e, acceptance-nodes
# (acceptance --nodes local), update.

# ---- the selection itself, the build and the toolchain: everything ----
ci/affected.py                     | all | all
ci/affected.map                    | all | all
ci/gates.sh                        | all | all
.github/**                         | all | all
Cargo.toml                         | all | all
Cargo.lock                         | all | all
rust-toolchain.toml                | all | all
rustfmt.toml                       | all | all
.cargo/**                          | all | all
.config/nextest.toml               | all | all
third_party/**                     | all | all

# ---- documentation ----
**/*.md                            | -   | docs
docs/**                            | -   | docs
